# Config for the Spacory Product / Engineer agents. dispatch.sh sources this
# file (exported) so every value here is inherited by the run-*.sh children and
# the headless Claude sessions they launch. This is the single place to configure
# an unattended agent run.
#
# SETUP: copy this file to ".agents/.env" (which is gitignored) and fill in real
# values. Never put real credentials in this template or in the *-agent-prompt.md
# files — those are committed to the repo.
#
#   cp .agents/.env.example .agents/.env
#
# In CI, do NOT use this file — inject the secrets as repository secrets instead.

# ── Telegram wrap-up notifications (notify.sh) ───────────────────────────────
# - TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: create a bot via @BotFather and paste the token it returns.
# - TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID:   message your bot, then read result[].message.chat.id from
#                       https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
# See .agents/README.md for the full walkthrough.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── Model & permissions (run-*.sh) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# CLAUDE_MODEL (--model) and CLAUDE_EFFORT (--effort) for the headless agents.
# "sonnet" at "medium": each run is bounded code generation / agentic tool use (one
# issue → PR, a review, a triage), which Anthropic's model guide maps to Sonnet 5 —
# not Opus, which it reserves for multihour autonomous agents and large refactors.
# Effort is a better lever than the model here: medium suits these small,
# well-specified tickets (xhigh is Opus's coding setting, and Sonnet@xhigh just
# converges to Opus cost for less); raise effort if review rounds climb. Escalate to
# "opus" only for a genuinely large / long-running ticket. Unset either → CLI default.
CLAUDE_MODEL=sonnet
CLAUDE_EFFORT=medium

# CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE: default "acceptEdits". Use "bypassPermissions" for
# fully unattended runs where a needed command isn't allowlisted in
# .claude/settings.json (only in a trusted environment).
#CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE=acceptEdits

# ── Dispatch pipeline (dispatch.sh) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# SPACORY_MAX_ROUNDS: resolve↔review rounds before a PR is marked blocked
# (default 5). Counted since the linked issue's body was last edited.
#SPACORY_MAX_ROUNDS=5

# SPACORY_AUTOMERGE: "1" to squash-merge an accepted PR once CI is green.
# Default off — the agents never self-merge; this is a human opt-in.
#SPACORY_AUTOMERGE=0
#
# SPACORY_CYCLE_LOCK_WAIT_SECS: how long the once-a-day product cycle waits for
# the shared dispatch lock before forfeiting its slot (default 1800 = 30m). The
# fast tick never waits — it retries on its next ~10-min fire — but the cycle
# would otherwise lose a whole day to a concurrent tick, so it waits.
#SPACORY_CYCLE_LOCK_WAIT_SECS=1800
#
# SPACORY_AGENT_RETRIES: extra attempts for an agent run that exits non-zero
# before the ticket is blocked (default 1 → 2 attempts total). A non-zero exit is
# always an infra fault (a stalled API stream, a killed process) — never a "changes
# requested" verdict, which is a parsed comment on a clean exit — so a retry only
# re-attempts a transient fault and can't mask a real rejection. 0 = block on first
# failure.
#SPACORY_AGENT_RETRIES=1
#
# SPACORY_AGENT_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECS: seconds to wait between those attempts
# (default 20).
#SPACORY_AGENT_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECS=20
